# Project Rules

## Project Type

This is a template repository for solo developers using AI coding tools. It is NOT a business application.

DO NOT create React/Vue/Electron apps, backend services, or CLI tools as part of this template.

## Core Philosophy

```
Repository manages state, AI manages execution, CI manages quality, Human manages decisions.
```

The goal is NOT to make AI write more code, but to make AI write more maintainable code within clear boundaries and quality rules.

## Required Reading

Before editing any code, read in order:

1. README.md
2. docs/00_project_brief.md
3. docs/04_architecture.md
4. docs/05_module_boundaries.md
5. docs/06_coding_standards.md
6. docs/07_testing_strategy.md
7. Current Issue or task description

## Rules

1. Do NOT code from vague requirements. Output a plan first.
2. Do NOT expand task scope without permission.
3. Do NOT refactor unrelated code.
4. Do NOT introduce new dependencies without justification.
5. Do NOT bypass tests.
6. Do NOT modify files outside the task scope.
7. STOP and ask when uncertain.
8. After changes, always report: what files changed, why, test results, risks.

## Language

Documentation and comments should be primarily in Chinese, with technical terms in English where appropriate.
